MARTIAL LAW ORDER
MARTIAL LAW ORDER
By
CHIEF MARTIAL LAW ADMINISTRATOR
No. 72
[20th October 1979]
1. In Martial Law Order No. 4,
hereinafter referred to as the said Order, in paragraph (2), for sub-paragraph
(1), the following shall be substituted and shall be deemed to have always been
so substituted :-
"(1) A Military Court shall
have power and jurisdiction to try and punish any person for offences under any
Martial Law Regulation, Martial Law Order, or under any of the under-mentioned
laws notwithstanding that an offence is triable exclusively by a Special Court
or Tribunal or Special Judge or any other authority or body :-
(a) Pakistan Penal Code (Act XLV
of 1860) ;
(b) President's Order No. 16 of
1977 ;
(c) The Foreign Exchange
Regulation Act, 1947 (XII of 1947) ;
(d) The Income-tax Act, 1922 (XI
of 1922) ;
(e) The Income-tax Ordinance,
1979 (XXXI of 1979) ;
(f) The offences specified in the
Schedule to the Pakistan Criminal Law (Amendment) Act, 1958 (XI, of 1958) ;
(g) The Customs Act, 1969 (IV of
1969) ;
(h) The Prevention of
Anti-National Activities Act, 1974 (VII of 1974) ;
(j) The Suppression of Terrorist
Activities (Special Courts) Act, 1975 (XV of 1975) ;
(k) The Prevention of Smuggling
Act, 1977 (XII of 1977) ;
(l) The Emigration Ordinance, 1979
(XVIII of 1979) ;
(m) The Explosive Substance Act,
1908 (VI of 1908) ;
(n) The Explosives Act, 1884 (IV
of 1884) ;
(o) The Foodstuff Control Act,
1958 (XX of 1958) ;
(p) The Punjab Excise Act, 1914
(I of 1914) ;
(q) The Opium Act, 1878 (1 of
1878) ;
(r) The Drugs Act, 1976 (XXX) of
1976) ;
(s) The Pakistan Essential
Services (Maintenance) Act, 1952 (LIII of 1952) ;
(t) The West Pakistan Essential
Articles Control Act, 1958 (XI of 1958) ;
(u) The West Pakistan,
Suppression of Prostitution Ordinance, 1961 (II of 1961);
(v) The Essential Commodities
Act, 1957 (Act No. III of 1957) ;
(w) The West Pakistan Arms
Ordinance, 1965 (XX of 1965) ;
(x) The Price Control and
Prevention of Profiteering and Hoarding Act, 1977 (Act No. XXIX of 1977) ;
(y) The Hoarding and Black
Marketing Order, 1956 (P. O. No. XIV of 1956) ;
(z) The Dangerous Drugs Act, 1930
(Act No. II of 1930) ;
(aa) The West Pakistan Pure Food
Ordinance, 1960 (Order No. VII of 1960) ;
(bb) The Sind Prevention of
Gambling Ordinance, 1978 (Ordinance No. V of 1978) ;
(cc) The Sind Standard Weights
and Measures (Enforcement) Act, 1975 (Act No. XX of 1975) ;
(dd) The Sind Pure Food
Ordinance,' 1960 (W. P. Ordinance No. VII of 1960) ;
(ee) Provincials Motor Vehicles
Ordinance, 1965 (W. P. Ordinance No. XIX of 1965);
(ff) The Sind Crime Control Act,
1975 (Act No. IV of 1975);
(gg) The West Pakistan Control of
Goondas Ordinance, 1969 (W. P. Ordinance No. XXXV of 1969);
(hh) The West Pakistan Border
Areas Foodstuffs (Control) Order, 1958;
(jj) Land Reforms Act, 1977 (Act
II of 1977);
(kk) Land Reforms Regulation,
1972 [Martial Law Regulation No. 115]."
2. In the said Order after
paragraph 3, the following new paragraph 3-A shall be inserted and shall be
deemed to have always been so inserted, namely :--
"3-A. No Court, including a
High Court, shall grant an injunction, make any order or entertain any
proceedings in respect of any matter to which the jurisdiction of a Military
Court or Tribunal extends and of which cognizance has been taken by, or which
has been transferred to, such Military Court or Tribunal and all proceedings in
respect of any such matter which may be pending before such other Court, other
than an appeal pending before the Supreme Court, shall abate."
